{"name":"La Paz Siesta","hex":"#c1e5ea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Pankararú."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paz"},{"term":"siesta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A nap, especially an afternoon one taken during the hottest part of the day in some cultures.","Laid-back attitudes to work or laziness, especially by a Hispanic person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take a siesta; to nap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/siesta"}],"entries":[{"title":"La Paz","blocks":[{"text":"La Paz, officially Nuestra Señora de La Paz, is the seat of government of Bolivia. With 755,732 residents as of 2024, it is the third-most populous city in Bolivia. Its metropolitan area, which includes the neighboring city of El Alto, and other smaller towns, is the second most populous urban area in Bolivia, with a population of 2.2 million, after Santa Cruz de la Sierra with a population of 2.3 million. The city is also the capital of the department of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Vista_del_centro_de_La_Paz.jpg/330px-Vista_del_centro_de_La_Paz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Paz","wikidata":"Q1491"},{"title":"Siesta","blocks":[{"text":"A midday nap is a short nap taken in the early afternoon, often after the midday meal. It is frequently referred to by its Spanish name siesta."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Noon%2C_rest_from_work_-_Van_Gogh.jpeg/330px-Noon%2C_rest_from_work_-_Van_Gogh.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siesta","wikidata":"Q203324"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Plaza_Murillo_en_La_Paz_-_Bolivia.jpg/500px-Plaza_Murillo